}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Michelia CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Naptime Michelia CC''' at level 30 by using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Michelia's range is her main limiting factor, making her less viable against [[Othom]], [[Mega-Mooth]] or units that push forward easily. Against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies like [[Shy Boy]], [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Bun]] and their respective variants, however, she tends to do an amazing job, both dealing fine damage and hindering their progress. [[Brollow]] is yet another enemy that can be countered very well by Michelia thanks to her fast animation and strength ability.

This unit can also be used as a viable generalist in early-mid game, but falls short later on due to her stats not making up for her range unless against Floating.

==='''Talents'''===
Michelia's talents breathe new life into this unit and make her pretty viable.

The main interest to consider here is the combination of '''Target Relic''' and '''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immune]]'''.  With this, Michelia now has a whole new world of target traits to [[Freeze|Freeze]] and deal high damage against. While her Freeze only lasts four seconds, not even hitting 50% uptime, it still serves as incredibly strong CC for Relics. With this, Michelia can deal huge damage against nasty Relic bosses such as [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]] or [[Relic Bun-Bun|Relic Bun-Bun]] and Freeze them in their tracks, meaning that she should obliterate most Relics in {{1c}} UL. While you might assume that Michelia can be thrown into the Labyrinth fodder bin after obtaining powerful UL Legends or [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]], her damage is surprisingly high, allowing her to have more DPS against Relic enemies than [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Storm Beast Naala]]. In addition, Michelia's Freeze has a unique coverage over Uril's Slow, meaning that on stages like Gigahaniwan, you can use Michelia alongside [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] to Freeze Gigahaniwan for comedic lengths of time and allow your rusher options to deal ridiculous amounts of damage.

'''Cost Down''', while not revolutionary, does help her a ton, bringing her cost down to only 3600c and making her very easy to deploy early on, especially on cash-tight stages which UL encourages.

Finally, Michelia has her stat talents. Michelia's main flaw is her health, which can easily be teared through even with [[Strong Against]] as she has no immunities to methods of pierce such as Wave or Surge. Because of this, if you really like Michelia you can probably invest in her '''Health Buff''' Talent, and leave her '''Attack Buff''' Talent for later. Be sure to invest into her with Catseyes before spending such a hefty NP cost on these Talents though.

Overall, Michelia's Talents make her genuinely viable against Relics, even in the face of competition from Uril and UL Legends. While you might be hesitant to Talent her if you've already cleared UL, for those just starting the journey Michelia isn't a bad choice to get whatsoever.

